## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design a robust real-time feature with offline resilience, data integrity, and testability in iOS, leveraging URLSessionWebSocketTask, GRDB, and atomic writes. Includes reconnect, deduplication, and replay logic.

## Key Concepts
- WebSocket lifecycle and backpressure management
- SQLite/GRDB transactions and schema design
- In-order delivery via sequence IDs
- Crash-safe resume and offline fallback
- Testing strategies for network faults and edge cases

## Code Example
```swift
// Sketch: minimal types and persistence
struct Comment: Codable {
    let id: String
    let seq: Int
    let author: String
    let content: String
    let createdAt: Date
}

class CommentFeed {
    private let db: DatabaseQueue
    private var socket: URLSessionWebSocketTask?
    private var lastSeq: Int = 0

    func connect() {
        socket = URLSession.shared.webSocketTask(with: URL(string: "wss://api.example.com/comments")!)
        socket?.resume()
        receiveMessages()
    }

    private func receiveMessages() {
        socket?.receive { [weak self] result in
            guard let self = self else { return }

            switch result {
            case .success(let message):
                self.handleMessage(message)
                self.receiveMessages()
            case .failure(let error):
                self.handleReconnection()
            }
        }
    }

    private func handleMessage(_ message: URLSessionWebSocketTask.Message) {
        // Parse and persist comment
    }
}
```

